# Cloudflare Pages redirects — ported from the "redirects" block in firebase.json,
# which production (Cloudflare Pages, see .github/workflows/deploy.yml) never reads.
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>. First match wins.
#
# Destinations use the trailing-slash form Cloudflare serves prerendered pages
# on (see src/lib/siteUrl.mjs), so a redirected visitor or crawler lands on a
# 200 in one hop instead of 301 -> 308 -> 200.
#
# SPA fallback needs no rule here: with no 404.html in dist, Cloudflare Pages
# serves index.html for unknown paths, which is what firebase.json's rewrites did.

